Enable the INA219 now that it is detected on the bus

The module was miswired; after fixing it the scan shows 0x3C, 0x40 and
0x76 and the chip reads back correctly ([ina] ok=1).

- ENABLE_INA219 -> 1.
- BATTERY_MIN_PLAUSIBLE_V (6.0 V): the failsafe now ignores voltage
  readings below any real 4S pack. Without Vin+/Vin- wired the INA219
  reads ~0.9 V, which would otherwise be taken as a flat battery and
  block arming. A missing sensor now means "no voltage protection"
  instead of a false "battery critical".

Firmware builds, 136/136 host tests pass.

